      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'keeping your dishwasher clean will make it last longer', as the phrase 'your dishwasher' directly addresses the user, implying that the advice is for the viewer to apply to their own appliance. The user is not projected onto the visual material (the person loading dishes) or the scene itself, but rather onto the instructional text, which is framed as a personal directive.",
